# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game"
msgstr "CHSH 게임"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"The last example to be discussed in this lesson is not a protocol, but a *game* known as the\n"
"*CHSH game*.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"이번 레슨에서 다룰 마지막 예제는 프로토콜이 아니라, *CHSH 게임*이라고 알려진 *게임*입니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When we speak of a game in this context, we're not talking about something that's meant to be played for fun or sport, but rather a mathematical abstraction in the sense of *game theory*.\n"
"Mathematical abstractions of games are studied in economics and computer science, for instance, and they are both fascinating and useful.\n"
msgstr ""
"여기서 게임이라고 할 때, 재미나 스포츠를 위해 즐기는 무언가를 뜻하는 것이 아니라, *게임 이론*의 의미에서 수학적 추상화를 가리킵니다.\n"
"게임의 수학적 추상화는 예를 들어 경제학이나 컴퓨터 과학에서 연구되며, 매우 흥미롭고 유용합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The letters CHSH refer to the authors — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony, and Richard Holt — of a 1969 paper where the example was first described.\n"
"They did not describe the example as a game, but rather as an experiment.\n"
"Its description as a game, however, is both natural and intuitive.\n"
msgstr ""
"CHSH라는 글자는 1969년 논문의 저자들 — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony, Richard Holt — 의 이름에서 따온 것으로, 이 논문에서 해당 예제가 처음 소개되었습니다.\n"
"그들은 이 예제를 게임이 아닌 실험으로 기술했습니다.\n"
"하지만 게임으로 설명하는 것이 자연스럽고 직관적입니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CHSH game falls within a class of games known as *nonlocal games*.\n"
"Nonlocal games are incredibly interesting and have deep connections to physics, computer science, and mathematics — holding mysteries that still remain unsolved.\n"
"We'll begin the section by explaining what nonlocal games are, and then we'll focus in on the CHSH game and what makes it interesting.\n"
msgstr ""
"CHSH 게임은 *비국소 게임(nonlocal games)*이라고 알려진 게임 분류에 속합니다.\n"
"비국소 게임은 매우 흥미롭고 물리학, 컴퓨터 과학, 수학과 깊은 연관이 있으며, 아직 해결되지 않은 미스터리를 품고 있습니다.\n"
"이 섹션에서는 먼저 비국소 게임이 무엇인지 설명한 뒤, CHSH 게임과 그 흥미로운 점에 집중하겠습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nonlocal games {#nonlocal-games}"
msgstr "비국소 게임 {#nonlocal-games}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A nonlocal game is a *cooperative game* where two players, Alice and Bob, work together to achieve a particular outcome.\n"
"The game is run by a *referee*, who behaves according to strict guidelines that are known to Alice and Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"비국소 게임은 두 플레이어, Alice와 Bob이 특정 결과를 달성하기 위해 협력하는 *협력 게임*입니다.\n"
"게임은 *심판*이 진행하며, 심판은 Alice와 Bob이 알고 있는 엄격한 규칙에 따라 행동합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob can prepare for the game however they choose, but once the game starts they are *forbidden from communicating*.\n"
"We might imagine the game taking place in a secure facility of some sort — as if the referee is playing the role of a detective and Alice and Bob are suspects being interrogated in different rooms.\n"
"But another way to think about the set-up is that Alice and Bob are separated by a vast distance, and communication is prohibited because the speed of light doesn't allow for it within the running time of the game.\n"
"That is to say, if Alice tries to send a message to Bob, the game will be over by the time he receives it, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice와 Bob은 원하는 방식으로 게임을 준비할 수 있지만, 게임이 시작되면 *서로 소통이 금지*됩니다.\n"
"마치 심판이 탐정 역할을 하고 Alice와 Bob이 각각 다른 방에서 심문받는 용의자처럼, 게임이 일종의 보안 시설에서 진행된다고 상상할 수 있습니다.\n"
"또는 Alice와 Bob이 아주 먼 거리에 떨어져 있어, 게임 진행 시간 내에 빛의 속도로도 통신이 불가능하기 때문에 소통이 금지된다고 생각할 수도 있습니다.\n"
"즉, Alice가 Bob에게 메시지를 보내려 해도, 그가 수신할 때쯤에는 게임이 이미 끝나 있을 것이고, 그 반대도 마찬가지입니다.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way a nonlocal game works is that the referee first asks each of Alice and Bob a question.\n"
"We'll use the letter $x$ to refer to Alice's question and $y$ to refer to Bob's question.\n"
"Here we're thinking of $x$ and $y$ as being classical states, and in the CHSH game $x$ and $y$ are bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"비국소 게임(nonlocal game)이 작동하는 방식은 심판이 먼저 Alice와 Bob 각각에게 질문을 하는 것입니다.\n"
"문자 $x$는 Alice의 질문을 나타내고 $y$는 Bob의 질문을 나타내는 데 사용하겠습니다.\n"
"여기서 $x$와 $y$는 고전 상태로 생각하며, CHSH 게임에서 $x$와 $y$는 비트입니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee uses *randomness* to select these questions.\n"
"To be precise, there is some probability $p(x,y)$ associated with each possible pair $(x,y)$ of questions, and the referee has vowed to choose the questions randomly, at the time of the game, in this way.\n"
"Everyone, including Alice and Bob, knows these probabilities — but nobody knows specifically which pair $(x,y)$ will be chosen until the game begins.\n"
msgstr ""
"심판은 *무작위성*을 사용하여 질문을 선택합니다.\n"
"정확히 말하면, 가능한 질문 쌍 $(x,y)$ 각각에 대해 확률 $p(x,y)$가 있으며, 심판은 게임 시점에 이 확률에 따라 무작위로 질문을 선택하기로 약속되어 있습니다.\n"
"Alice와 Bob을 포함하여 모든 사람이 이 확률을 알고 있지만, 게임이 시작되기 전까지는 어떤 쌍 $(x,y)$이 선택될지 아무도 모릅니다.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After Alice and Bob receive their questions, they must then provide answers: Alice's answer is $a$ and Bob's answer is $b$.\n"
"Again, these are classical states in general, and bits in the CHSH game.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice와 Bob이 질문을 받은 후, 각자 답변을 제시해야 합니다. Alice의 답변은 $a$, Bob의 답변은 $b$입니다.\n"
"마찬가지로 이것들도 일반적으로는 고전 상태이며, CHSH 게임에서는 비트입니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point the referee makes a decision: Alice and Bob either *win* or *lose* depending on whether or not the pair of answers $(a,b)$ is deemed correct for the pair of questions $(x,y)$ according to some fixed set of rules.\n"
"Different rules mean different games, and the rules for the CHSH game specifically are described in the section following this one.\n"
"As was already suggested, the rules are known to everyone.\n"
msgstr ""
"이 시점에서 심판은 결정을 내립니다. 답변 쌍 $(a,b)$가 어떤 고정된 규칙에 따라 질문 쌍 $(x,y)$에 대해 올바른지 아닌지에 따라 Alice와 Bob이 *이기거나 지게* 됩니다.\n"
"규칙이 다르면 게임도 달라지며, CHSH 게임에 대한 구체적인 규칙은 다음 섹션에서 설명합니다.\n"
"앞서 언급했듯이, 규칙은 모든 사람에게 알려져 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following diagram provides a graphic representation of the interactions.\n"
msgstr "다음 다이어그램은 이 상호작용을 그림으로 나타낸 것입니다.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is the uncertainty about which questions will be asked, and specifically the fact that each player doesn't know the other player's question, that makes nonlocal games challenging for Alice and Bob — just like colluding suspects in different rooms trying to keep their story straight.\n"
msgstr "어떤 질문이 주어질지 불확실하고, 특히 각 플레이어가 상대방의 질문을 모른다는 점이 Alice와 Bob에게 비국소 게임을 어렵게 만듭니다 — 마치 각자 다른 방에 있는 공모 용의자들이 진술을 맞추려는 것처럼 말이지요.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A precise description of the referee defines an instance of a nonlocal game.\n"
"This includes a specification of the probabilities $p(x,y)$ for each question pair along with the rules\n"
"that determine whether each pair of answers $(a,b)$ wins or loses for each possible question pair $(x,y)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"심판에 대한 정확한 설명이 비국소 게임의 하나의 인스턴스를 정의합니다.\n"
"여기에는 각 질문 쌍의 확률 $p(x,y)$ 명세와, 가능한 질문 쌍 $(x,y)$ 각각에 대해 답변 쌍 $(a,b)$가 이기는지 지는지를 결정하는 규칙이 포함됩니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll take a look at the CHSH game momentarily, but before that let us briefly acknowledge that it's also interesting to consider other nonlocal games.\n"
"It's extremely interesting, in fact, and there are some nonlocal games for which it's currently not known how well Alice and Bob can play using entanglement.\n"
"The set-up is simple, but there's complexity at work — and for some games it can be impossibly difficult to compute best or near-best strategies for Alice and Bob.\n"
"This is the mind-blowing nature of the non-local games model.\n"
msgstr ""
"잠시 후 CHSH 게임을 살펴보겠지만, 그에 앞서 다른 비국소 게임들도 흥미롭다는 점을 간략히 짚고 넘어가겠습니다.\n"
"사실 이것은 매우 흥미로운 주제이며, 엉킴(얽힘)을 사용했을 때 Alice와 Bob이 얼마나 잘 플레이할 수 있는지 현재까지 알려지지 않은 비국소 게임들도 있습니다.\n"
"설정은 단순하지만 그 안에는 복잡성이 내재되어 있으며, 일부 게임에서는 Alice와 Bob의 최선 또는 최선에 근접한 전략을 계산하는 것이 불가능할 정도로 어렵습니다.\n"
"이것이 비국소 게임 모델의 놀라운 본질입니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game description {#chsh-game-description}"
msgstr "CHSH 게임 설명 {#chsh-game-description}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is the precise description of the CHSH game, where (as above) $x$ is Alice's question, $y$ is Bob's question, $a$ is Alice's answer, and $b$ is Bob's answer:\n"
msgstr "다음은 CHSH 게임의 정확한 설명입니다. 여기서 (위와 같이) $x$는 Alice의 질문, $y$는 Bob의 질문, $a$는 Alice의 답변, $b$는 Bob의 답변입니다.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The questions and answers are all bits: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}$.\n"
msgstr "질문과 답변은 모두 비트입니다: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The referee chooses the questions $(x,y)$ *uniformly at random*. That is, each of the four possibilities, $(0,0)$, $(0,1)$, $(1,0)$, and $(1,1)$, is selected with probability $1/4$.\n"
msgstr "심판은 질문 $(x,y)$를 *균등 무작위로* 선택합니다. 즉, 네 가지 가능성 $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0),$ $(1,1)$ 각각이 확률 $1/4$로 선택됩니다.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The answers $(a,b)$ *win* for the questions $(x,y)$ if $a\\oplus b = x\\wedge y$ and *lose* otherwise. The following table expresses this rule by listing the winning and losing conditions on the answers $(a,b)$ for each pair of questions $(x,y)$.\n"
msgstr "답변 $(a,b)$는 $a\\oplus b = x\\wedge y$이면 질문 $(x,y)$에 대해 *이기고*, 그렇지 않으면 *집니다*. 다음 표는 각 질문 쌍 $(x,y)$에 대해 답변 $(a,b)$의 이기는 조건과 지는 조건을 나열하여 이 규칙을 표현합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Limitation of classical strategies {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"
msgstr "고전 전략의 한계 {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's consider strategies for Alice and Bob in the CHSH game, beginning with *classical* strategies.\n"
msgstr "이제 CHSH 게임에서 Alice와 Bob의 전략을 살펴보겠습니다. 먼저 *고전* 전략부터 시작합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deterministic strategies {#deterministic-strategies}"
msgstr "결정론적 전략 {#deterministic-strategies}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll start with *deterministic* strategies, where Alice's answer $a$ is a function of the question $x$ that she receives, and likewise Bob's answer $b$ is a function of the question $y$ he receives.\n"
"So, for instance, we may write $a(0)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $0$, and $a(1)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"먼저 *결정론적* 전략을 다루겠습니다. 여기서 Alice의 답변 $a$는 그녀가 받는 질문 $x$의 함수이고, 마찬가지로 Bob의 답변 $b$는 그가 받는 질문 $y$의 함수입니다.\n"
"예를 들어, Alice의 질문이 $0$일 때의 답변은 $a(0)$으로, 질문이 $1$일 때의 답변은 $a(1)$로 표기할 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No deterministic strategy can possibly win the CHSH game every time.\n"
"One way to reason this is simply to go one-by-one through all of the possible deterministic strategies and check that every one of them loses for at least one of the four possible question pairs.\n"
"Alice and Bob can each choose from four possible functions from one bit to one bit — which we encountered back in the first lesson of the course — so there are $16$ different deterministic strategies in total to check.\n"
msgstr ""
"어떤 결정론적 전략도 CHSH 게임을 항상 이길 수는 없습니다.\n"
"한 가지 논증 방법은 모든 가능한 결정론적 전략을 하나씩 검토하여, 그 중 어느 것도 네 가지 가능한 질문 쌍 중 적어도 하나에서는 진다는 것을 확인하는 것입니다.\n"
"Alice와 Bob 각자는 1비트에서 1비트로 가는 네 가지 가능한 함수 중 하나를 선택할 수 있으며 — 이는 강좌의 첫 번째 레슨에서 다뤘습니다 — 따라서 확인해야 할 결정론적 전략은 총 $16$가지입니다.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also reason this analytically.\n"
"If Alice and Bob's strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,0)$, then it must be that $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"if their strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,1)$, then $a(0) = b(1)$; and similarly,\n"
"if the strategy wins for $(x,y)=(1,0)$ then $a(1) = b(0)$.\n"
"So, if their strategy wins for all three possibilities, then\n"
msgstr ""
"이를 분석적으로도 논증할 수 있습니다.\n"
"Alice와 Bob의 전략이 $(x,y) = (0,0)$일 때 이기려면 $a(0) = b(0)$이어야 하고,\n"
"$(x,y) = (0,1)$일 때 이기려면 $a(0) = b(1)$이어야 하며,\n"
"마찬가지로 $(x,y)=(1,0)$일 때 이기려면 $a(1) = b(0)$이어야 합니다.\n"
"따라서 세 가지 경우 모두에서 이기는 전략이 있다면,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that the strategy loses in the final case $(x,y) = (1,1)$, for here winning requires that\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1)$.\n"
"Thus, there can be no deterministic strategy that wins every time.\n"
msgstr ""
"이는 마지막 경우 $(x,y) = (1,1)$에서 전략이 진다는 것을 의미합니다. 이 경우 이기려면\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1)$이어야 하기 때문입니다.\n"
"따라서 항상 이기는 결정론적 전략은 존재하지 않습니다.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it is easy to find deterministic strategies that win in three of the four cases, such as $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0$.\n"
"From this we conclude that the maximum probability for Alice and Bob to win using a deterministic strategy is $3/4$.\n"
msgstr ""
"반면$,a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0$처럼 네 가지 경우 중 세 가지에서 이기는 결정론적 전략은 쉽게 찾을 수 있습니다.\n"
"이를 통해 결정론적 전략을 사용했을 때 Alice와 Bob이 이길 수 있는 최대 확률은 $3/4$임을 알 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic strategies {#probabilistic-strategies}"
msgstr "확률론적 전략 {#probabilistic-strategies}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we just concluded, Alice and Bob cannot do better than winning the CHSH game 75% of the time using a deterministic strategy.\n"
"But what about a probabilistic strategy?\n"
"Could it help Alice and Bob to use randomness — including the possibility of *shared randomness*, where their random choices are correlated?\n"
msgstr ""
"방금 결론 내렸듯이, Alice와 Bob은 결정론적 전략을 사용하면 CHSH 게임에서 75%보다 높은 승률을 달성할 수 없습니다.\n"
"그렇다면 확률론적 전략은 어떨까요?\n"
"무작위성을 사용하는 것 — *공유 무작위성(shared randomness)*, 즉 무작위 선택이 서로 상관되는 경우를 포함하여 — 이 도움이 될 수 있을까요?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It turns out that probabilistic strategies don't help at all to increase the probability that Alice and Bob win.\n"
"This is because every probabilistic strategy can alternatively be viewed as a random selection of a deterministic strategy, just like probabilistic operations can be viewed as random selections of deterministic operations.\n"
"The average is never larger than the maximum, and so it follows that probabilistic strategies don't offer any advantage in terms of their overall winning probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"결론적으로 확률론적 전략은 Alice와 Bob의 승률을 높이는 데 전혀 도움이 되지 않습니다.\n"
"이는 모든 확률론적 전략이 결정론적 전략의 무작위 선택으로 볼 수 있기 때문입니다. 마치 확률론적 연산이 결정론적 연산의 무작위 선택으로 볼 수 있는 것처럼 말이지요.\n"
"평균은 최대값을 절대 초과하지 않으므로, 확률론적 전략은 전체 승률 면에서 어떠한 이점도 제공하지 않습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, winning with probability $3/4$ is the best that Alice and Bob can do using any classical strategy, whether deterministic or probabilistic.\n"
msgstr "따라서 확률론적이든 결정론적이든 어떤 고전 전략을 사용해도 Alice와 Bob이 달성할 수 있는 최선은 $3/4$의 승률입니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game strategy {#chsh-game-strategy}"
msgstr "CHSH 게임 전략 {#chsh-game-strategy}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A natural question to ask at this point is whether Alice and Bob can do any better using a *quantum* strategy.\n"
"In particular, if they share an entangled quantum state as the following figure suggests, which they could have prepared prior to playing the game, can they increase their winning probability?\n"
msgstr ""
"이 시점에서 자연스럽게 떠오르는 질문은, Alice와 Bob이 *양자* 전략을 사용하면 더 잘할 수 있는가 하는 것입니다.\n"
"특히 다음 그림처럼 그들이 게임을 시작하기 전에 준비해 둔 얽힘 양자 상태를 공유하고 있다면, 승률을 높일 수 있을까요?\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game-entanglement.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game-entanglement.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answer is yes, and this is the main point of the example and why it's so interesting.\n"
"So let's see exactly how Alice and Bob can do better in this game using entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"대답은 '그렇다'이며, 이것이 이 예제의 핵심이자 흥미로운 이유입니다.\n"
"그렇다면 Alice와 Bob이 얽힘을 사용하여 이 게임에서 어떻게 더 잘할 수 있는지 살펴보겠습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Required vectors and matrices {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"
msgstr "필요한 벡터와 행렬 {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first thing we need to do is to define a qubit state vector $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$, for each real number\n"
"$\\theta$ (which we'll think of as an angle measured in radians) as follows.\n"
msgstr "먼저 각 실수 $\\theta$ (라디안 단위의 각도로 생각합니다)에 대해 qubit 상태 벡터 $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$를 다음과 같이 정의합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here are some simple examples:\n"
msgstr "몇 가지 간단한 예시는 다음과 같습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We also have the following examples, which arise in the analysis below:\n"
msgstr "아래 분석에서 등장하는 다음 예시들도 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Looking at the general form, we see that the inner product between any two of these vectors has this formula:\n"
msgstr "일반적인 형태를 살펴보면, 이 벡터들 사이의 내적은 다음 공식을 따릅니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In detail, there are only real number entries in these vectors, so there are no complex conjugates to worry about:\n"
"the inner product is the product of the cosines plus the product of the sines.\n"
"Using one of the *angle addition formulas* from trigonometry leads to the simplification above.\n"
"This formula reveals the geometric interpretation of the inner product between real unit vectors as the cosine of the angle between them.\n"
msgstr ""
"자세히 말하면, 이 벡터들의 원소는 모두 실수이므로 복소켤레를 걱정할 필요가 없습니다.\n"
"내적은 코사인의 곱과 사인의 곱의 합입니다.\n"
"삼각법의 *각도 덧셈 공식* 중 하나를 이용하면 위와 같이 단순화됩니다.\n"
"이 공식은 실수 단위 벡터 사이의 내적이 그 사이 각도의 코사인이라는 기하학적 해석을 드러냅니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we compute the inner product of the *tensor product* of any two of these vectors with the $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ state, we obtain a similar expression, except that it has a $\\sqrt{2}$ in the denominator:\n"
msgstr "이 벡터들 중 임의의 두 벡터의 *텐서곱*과 $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ 상태의 내적을 계산하면, 분모에 $\\sqrt{2}$가 있다는 점만 제외하고 비슷한 식을 얻습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our interest in this particular inner product will become clear shortly, but for now we're simply observing this as a formula.\n"
msgstr "이 특정 내적에 관심을 갖는 이유는 곧 명확해지겠지만, 지금은 단순히 공식으로 관찰하는 것으로 충분합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, define a unitary matrix $U_{\\theta}$ for each angle $\\theta$ as follows.\n"
msgstr "다음으로, 각 각도 $\\theta$에 대해 유니타리 행렬 $U_{\\theta}$를 다음과 같이 정의합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, this matrix transforms $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
"To check that this is a unitary matrix, a key observation is that the vectors $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ are orthogonal for every angle $\\theta$:\n"
msgstr ""
"직관적으로 말하면, 이 행렬은 $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$를 $\\vert 0\\rangle$으로$,\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$를 $\\vert 1\\rangle$로 변환합니다.\n"
"이것이 유니타리 행렬임을 확인하는 핵심 관찰은, 벡터 $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$와 $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$이 모든 각도 $\\theta$에 대해 직교한다는 것입니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, we find that\n"
msgstr "따라서 다음을 알 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We may alternatively write this matrix explicitly as\n"
msgstr "이 행렬을 명시적으로 나타내면 다음과 같습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is an example of a *rotation matrix*, and specifically it rotates two-dimensional vectors with real number entries by an angle of $-\\theta$ about the origin.\n"
"If we follow a standard convention for naming and parameterizing rotations of various forms, we have\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ where\n"
msgstr ""
"이것은 *회전 행렬*의 예시로, 구체적으로는 실수 원소를 가진 2차원 벡터를 원점 주위로 $-\\theta$만큼 회전시킵니다.\n"
"다양한 형태의 회전에 대한 표준 명명 및 매개변수화 관례를 따르면, $U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$이며 여기서\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Strategy description {#strategy-description}"
msgstr "전략 설명 {#strategy-description}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can describe the quantum strategy.\n"
msgstr "이제 양자 전략을 설명할 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Set-up:** Alice and Bob start the game sharing an e-bit: Alice holds a qubit $\\mathsf{A}$, Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B}$, and together the two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ are in the $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ state.\n"
msgstr "**준비:** Alice와 Bob은 e-비트를 공유하며 게임을 시작합니다. Alice는 qubit $\\mathsf{A}$를, Bob은 qubit $\\mathsf{B}$를 보유하고, 두 qubit $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$은 함께 $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ 상태에 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Alice's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Alice의 행동:**\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If Alice receives the question $x=0$, she applies $U_{0}$ to her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
msgstr "Alice가 질문 $x=0$을 받으면, 그녀의 qubit $\\mathsf{A}$에 $U_{0}$를 적용합니다.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If Alice receives the question  $x=1$, she applies $U_{\\pi/4}$ to her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
msgstr "Alice가 질문 $x=1$을 받으면, 그녀의 qubit $\\mathsf{A}$에 $U_{\\pi/4}$를 적용합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The operation Alice performs on $\\mathsf{A}$ may alternatively be described like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Alice가 $\\mathsf{A}$에 수행하는 연산은 다음과 같이 나타낼 수도 있습니다.\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
