"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The probabilities have effectively swapped places from in the three other cases.\n"
"   We obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   앞선 세 경우와 비교해 확률이 사실상 자리를 바꾼 형태입니다.\n"
"   합산하면 $a=b$일 확률과 $a\\neq b$일 확률은 다음과 같습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   For the question pair $(1,1)$, Alice and Bob win if $a\\neq b$, and therefore they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr "   질문 쌍 $(1,1)$에서는 $a\\neq b$이면 Alice와 Bob이 이기므로, 이 경우 이길 확률은 다음과 같습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "They win in every case with the same probability:\n"
msgstr "네 가지 경우 모두에서 이길 확률은 동일합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is therefore the probability that they win overall.\n"
"That's significantly better than any classical strategy can do for this game; classical strategies have winning probability bounded by $3/4$. And that makes this a very interesting example.\n"
msgstr ""
"따라서 이것이 전체적인 승리 확률입니다.\n"
"이는 어떤 고전적인 전략보다도 훨씬 높은 수치입니다. 고전적인 전략의 승리 확률은 $3/4$으로 제한되어 있기 때문입니다. 그래서 이 예제는 매우 흥미롭습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This happens to be the *optimal* winning probability for quantum strategies.\n"
"That is, we can't do any better than this, no matter what entangled state or measurements we choose.\n"
"This fact is known as *Tsirelson's inequality*, named for Boris Tsirelson who first proved it — and who first described the CHSH experiment as a game.\n"
msgstr ""
"이 확률은 양자 전략에서 *최적*의 승리 확률이기도 합니다.\n"
"즉, 어떤 얽힘 상태나 측정 방법을 선택하더라도 이보다 더 좋은 결과를 낼 수는 없습니다.\n"
"이 사실은 *Tsirelson의 부등식*으로 알려져 있으며, 이를 처음 증명하고 CHSH 실험을 게임으로 처음 묘사한 Boris Tsirelson의 이름을 따서 명명되었습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Geometric picture {#geometric-picture}"
msgstr "기하학적 그림 {#geometric-picture}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is possible to think about the strategy described above geometrically, which may be helpful for understanding the relationships among the various angles chosen for Alice and Bob's operations.\n"
msgstr "위에서 설명한 전략을 기하학적으로 생각해볼 수 있습니다. 이는 Alice와 Bob의 연산에서 선택한 다양한 각도 사이의 관계를 이해하는 데 도움이 될 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Alice effectively does is to choose an angle $\\alpha$, depending on her question $x$, and then to apply $U_{\\alpha}$ to her qubit and measure.\n"
"Similarly, Bob chooses an angle $\\beta$, depending on $y$, and then he applies $U_{\\beta}$ to his qubit and measures.\n"
"We've chosen $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ like so.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice가 실질적으로 하는 일은 질문 $x$에 따라 각도 $\\alpha$를 선택한 뒤, 자신의 Qubit에 $U_{\\alpha}$를 적용하고 측정하는 것입니다.\n"
"마찬가지로 Bob은 $y$에 따라 각도 $\\beta$를 선택한 뒤, 자신의 Qubit에 $U_{\\beta}$를 적용하고 측정합니다.\n"
"우리는 $\\alpha$와 $\\beta$를 다음과 같이 선택했습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\alpha & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"0 & x=0\\\\\n"
"\\pi/4 & x=1\n"
"\\end{cases}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\beta & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pi/8 & y = 0\\\\\n"
"-\\pi/8 & y = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\alpha & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"0 & x=0\\\\\n"
"\\pi/4 & x=1\n"
"\\end{cases}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\beta & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pi/8 & y = 0\\\\\n"
"-\\pi/8 & y = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the moment, though, let's take $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ to be arbitrary.\n"
"By choosing $\\alpha$, Alice effectively defines an orthonormal basis of vectors that looks like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"지금은 $\\alpha$와 $\\beta$를 임의의 값이라고 생각해봅시다.\n"
"Alice는 $\\alpha$를 선택함으로써 다음과 같이 생긴 정규직교 기저 벡터들을 효과적으로 정의합니다.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Basis for Alice](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/alpha-basis.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Basis for Alice](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/alpha-basis.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bob does likewise, except that his angle is $\\beta$:\n"
msgstr "Bob도 마찬가지이지만, 그의 각도는 $\\beta$입니다.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Basis for Bob](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/beta-basis.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Basis for Bob](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/beta-basis.avif)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The colors of the vectors correspond to Alice and Bob's answers: blue for $0$ and red for $1$.\n"
msgstr "벡터의 색깔은 Alice와 Bob의 답변에 대응합니다. 파란색은 $0$, 빨간색은 $1$입니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, if we combine together $(1)$ and $(2)$ we get the formula\n"
msgstr "이제 $(1)$과 $(2)$를 결합하면 다음 식을 얻습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which works for all real numbers $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$.\n"
msgstr "이 식은 모든 실수 $\\alpha$와 $\\beta$에 대해 성립합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Following the same sort of analysis that we went through above, but with $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ being variables, we find this:\n"
msgstr "위에서 진행한 분석과 동일한 방식으로, 단 $\\alpha$와 $\\beta$를 변수로 놓고 전개하면 다음을 얻습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & \\bigl(U_{\\alpha} \\otimes U_{\\beta}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad =\n"
"    \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta + \\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{\n"
"        \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 11\\rangle\n"
"      }{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & \\bigl(U_{\\alpha} \\otimes U_{\\beta}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad =\n"
"    \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta + \\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{\n"
"        \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 11\\rangle\n"
"      }{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We conclude these two formulas:\n"
msgstr "여기서 다음 두 공식을 도출할 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a = b)  & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\alpha - \\beta)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\sin^2(\\alpha - \\beta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a = b)  & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\alpha - \\beta)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\sin^2(\\alpha - \\beta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These equations can be connected to the figures above by imagining that we superimpose the bases chosen by Alice and Bob.\n"
"In particular, when $(x,y) = (0,0)$, Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = 0$ and $\\beta = \\pi/8$, and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"이 식들은 Alice와 Bob이 선택한 기저를 겹쳐 놓는 것으로 위의 그림들과 연결됩니다.\n"
"특히 $(x,y) = (0,0)$일 때 Alice와 Bob은 $\\alpha = 0$과 $\\beta = \\pi/8$을 선택하며, 두 기저를 겹치면 다음 그림을 얻습니다.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/strategy00.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/strategy00.avif)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angle between the red vectors is $\\pi/8$, which is the same as the angle between the two blue vectors.\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is the cosine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"빨간 벡터들 사이의 각도는 $\\pi/8$이며, 두 파란 벡터들 사이의 각도도 동일합니다.\n"
"Alice와 Bob의 측정 결과가 일치할 확률은 이 각도의 코사인 제곱으로,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "while the probability they disagree is the sine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr "결과가 다를 확률은 이 각도의 사인 제곱으로,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When $(x,y) = (0,1)$, Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = 0$ and $\\beta = -\\pi/8$, and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr "$(x,y) = (0,1)$일 때, Alice와 Bob은 $\\alpha = 0$과 $\\beta = -\\pi/8$을 선택하며, 이들의 기저를 겹쳐보면 다음 그림을 얻습니다.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/strategy01.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/strategy01.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angle between the red vectors is again $\\pi/8$, as is the angle between the blue vectors.\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is again the cosine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"빨간색 벡터 사이의 각도는 다시 $\\pi/8$이며, 파란색 벡터 사이의 각도도 마찬가지입니다.\n"
"Alice와 Bob의 결과가 일치할 확률은 다시 이 각도의 코사인 제곱입니다.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When $(x,y) = (1,0)$, Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ and $\\beta = \\pi/8$, and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr "$(x,y) = (1,0)$일 때, Alice와 Bob은 $\\alpha = \\pi/4$와 $\\beta = \\pi/8$을 선택하며, 이들의 기저를 겹쳐보면 다음 그림을 얻습니다.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/strategy10.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/strategy10.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bases have changed but the angles haven't — once again the angle between vectors of the same color is $\\pi/8$.\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is\n"
msgstr ""
"기저는 바뀌었지만 각도는 바뀌지 않았습니다 — 같은 색의 벡터 사이의 각도는 여전히 $\\pi/8$입니다.\n"
"Alice와 Bob의 결과가 일치할 확률은 다음과 같습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and the probability they disagree is\n"
msgstr ""
"기저는 바뀌었지만 각도는 변하지 않았습니다. 다시 한 번 같은 색 벡터들 사이의 각도는 $\\pi/8$입니다.\n"
"Alice와 Bob의 결과가 일치할 확률은\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When $(x,y) = (1,1)$, Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ and $\\beta = -\\pi/8$. When we superimpose their bases, we see that something different has happened:\n"
msgstr "$(x,y) = (1,1)$일 때, Alice와 Bob은 $\\alpha = \\pi/4$와 $\\beta = -\\pi/8$을 선택합니다. 이들의 기저를 겹쳐보면 무언가 다른 일이 일어난 것을 알 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/strategy11.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/strategy11.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the way the angles were chosen, this time the angle between vectors having the same color is $3\\pi/8$ rather than $\\pi/8$.\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is still the cosine-squared of this angle, but this time the value is\n"
msgstr ""
"각도가 선택된 방식 때문에, 이번에는 같은 색의 벡터 사이의 각도가 $\\pi/8$이 아니라 $3\\pi/8$입니다.\n"
"Alice와 Bob의 결과가 일치할 확률은 여전히 이 각도의 코사인 제곱이지만, 이번에는 값이 다음과 같습니다.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The probability the outcomes disagree is the sine-squared of this angle, which in this case is this:\n"
msgstr "결과가 일치하지 않을 확률은 이 각도의 사인 제곱이며, 이 경우 다음과 같습니다.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remarks {#remarks}"
msgstr "비고 {#remarks}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The basic idea of an experiment like the CHSH game, where entanglement leads to statistical results that are inconsistent with purely classical reasoning, is due to John Bell, the namesake of the Bell states.\n"
"For this reason, people often refer to experiments of this sort as *Bell tests*.\n"
"Sometimes people also refer to *Bell's theorem*, which can be formulated in different ways — but the essence of it is that quantum mechanics is not compatible with so-called *local hidden variable theories*.\n"
"The CHSH game is a particularly clean and simple example of a Bell test, and can be viewed as a proof, or demonstration, of Bell's theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"CHSH 게임과 같이 얽힘이 순전히 고전적인 추론으로는 설명할 수 없는 통계적 결과를 이끌어낸다는 실험의 기본 아이디어는 Bell 상태의 이름을 딴 존 벨(John Bell)에서 비롯되었습니다.\n"
"이러한 이유로 사람들은 이런 종류의 실험을 흔히 *벨 테스트(Bell test)*라고 부릅니다.\n"
"또한 *벨의 정리(Bell's theorem)*를 언급하기도 하는데, 이는 다양한 방식으로 표현될 수 있지만 — 그 본질은 양자역학이 이른바 *국소 숨은 변수 이론(local hidden variable theory)*과 양립하지 않는다는 것입니다.\n"
"CHSH 게임은 벨 테스트의 특히 명확하고 단순한 예이며, 벨의 정리에 대한 증명 또는 시연으로 볼 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CHSH game offers a way to experimentally test the theory of quantum information.\n"
"Experiments can be performed that implement the CHSH game, and test the sorts of strategies based on entanglement described above.\n"
"This provides us with a high degree of confidence that entanglement is real — and unlike the sometimes vague or poetic ways that we come up with to explain entanglement, the CHSH game gives us a concrete and testable way to *observe* entanglement.\n"
"The 2022 Nobel Prize in Physics acknowledges the importance of this line of work: the prize was awarded to Alain Aspect, John Clauser (the C in CHSH) and Anton Zeilinger for observing entanglement through Bell tests on entangled photons.\n"
msgstr ""
"CHSH 게임은 양자 정보 이론을 실험적으로 검증하는 방법을 제공합니다.\n"
"CHSH 게임을 구현하고, 위에서 설명한 얽힘 기반 전략들을 검증하는 실험을 수행할 수 있습니다.\n"
"이는 얽힘이 실재한다는 높은 수준의 확신을 제공합니다. 얽힘을 설명하는 때로는 모호하거나 시적인 표현들과 달리, CHSH 게임은 얽힘을 *관찰*할 수 있는 구체적이고 검증 가능한 방법을 제공합니다.\n"
"2022년 노벨 물리학상은 이 연구 흐름의 중요성을 인정합니다. 상은 알랭 아스페(Alain Aspect), 존 클라우저(John Clauser, CHSH의 C), 안톤 차일링거(Anton Zeilinger)에게 얽힌 광자를 이용한 벨 테스트를 통해 얽힘을 관찰한 공로로 수여되었습니다.\n"
